The issue is that your plotted “good” initial parameters are not the same parameters you are actually giving to `FindFit`.

In your code, you appear to be mixing:
- raw values in kHz,
- values in Hz,
- and angular frequencies like `2 π × frequency`.

That means the starting point you think is close is not actually close in the model space `FindFit` is optimizing over.

Key fix
- If the detuning offset is physically around `-91 kHz`, then in your function it should likely be entered as something like `-2 π 91 10^3`, not `-91`.
- Likewise, if your independent variable `Δ` is in kHz in the plot, but your model uses angular frequency, you should consistently scale it inside `FindFit`.

A corrected version would look like this:

```wl
scandata = Import["peakdata.csv"];
scandata = Map[{#[[1]], N[ToExpression[#[[2]]]]} &, scandata];

P1[Ω_, Δ_, t_] := ((Ω/Sqrt[Ω^2 + Δ^2])*Sin[(1/2)*Sqrt[Ω^2 + Δ^2]*t])^2;

fitfunction[Ω_, Δ_, t_, a_, b_, c_] := a + b*P1[Ω, Δ + c, t];

Ωapprox = 2 π 29 10^3;
centrepeak = -2 π 91 10^3;
amplitude = 0.8;
offset = 0.13;
pulsetime = 16 10^-6;

rabifit = 
 FindFit[
  scandata,
  {fitfunction[Ω, 2 π Δ 10^3, pulsetime, voffset, amp, hoffset],
   amp < 1, amp > 0, voffset > 0, voffset < 0.5},
  {{Ω, Ωapprox}, {amp, amplitude}, {voffset, offset}, {hoffset, centrepeak}},
  Δ,
  MaxIterations -> 1000
 ]
```

And when plotting, use the same scaling:

```wl
Show[
 Plot[
  {
   fitfunction[Ωapprox, 2 π Δ 10^3, pulsetime, offset, amplitude, centrepeak],
   fitfunction[Ω, 2 π Δ 10^3, pulsetime, voffset, amp, hoffset] /. rabifit
  },
  {Δ, 0, 200},
  PlotRange -> {All, {0, 1}},
  PlotStyle -> {Directive[Thick, Red], Directive[Thick, Orange]},
  Frame -> True,
  FrameLabel -> {"Frequency (kHz)", "Probability in |1>"}
 ],
 ListPlot[scandata, PlotStyle -> PointSize[0.007]]
]
```

Why this matters
`FindFit` is only as good as the parameterization you give it. If the model expects angular frequency but the initial guesses are in plain frequency units, the optimizer may converge to a mathematically valid but physically meaningless local minimum.

