But for different y-axes, a better pattern is to rescale one curve to match the other axis:

```mathematica
Plot[
 {f[x], Rescale[g[x], {y2min, y2max}, {y1min, y1max}]},
 {x, xmin, xmax},
 Frame -> True,
 FrameTicks -> {
   {Automatic, (Charting`ScaledTicks[{Identity, Identity}][#] & /@ {y2min, y2max})},
   {Automatic, Automatic}
 },
 PlotStyle -> {Blue, Red}
]
