`Image@Graphics[...]` is not the same as `Graphics[..., ImageSize -> ...]`.

`Graphics` produces a graphics expression, and `Image` then rasterizes that graphics using its own default image sizing behavior. So the text can get clipped because `Image` is doing the final sizing/cropping, not `Graphics`.

Use `Image`’s `ImageSize` option:

```wl
g = Graphics[
  {FontSize -> 20,
   Text["now is the time for all good men to come to the aid of their country"]}
];

Image[g, ImageSize -> {1000, 30}]
```

Or, if you want a `Graphics` with the intended dimensions before converting:

```wl
g = Graphics[
  {FontSize -> 20,
   Text["now is the time for all good men to come to the aid of their country"]},
  ImageSize -> {1000, 30}
];

Image[g]
```

In short: set the size on `Image` if you are converting `Graphics` to `Image`.

