To monitor the progress of importing files, use a separate progress variable and update it inside the import loop, rather than trying to attach `Monitor[]` directly to the import itself.

A typical pattern is:

```wolfram
progress = 0;
files = FileNames["*.csv", dir];
n = Length[files];

result = Table[
  progress = i/n;
  Import[files[[i]]],
  {i, n}
];

progress = 1;
```

Then display the progress with:

```wolfram
Dynamic[ProgressIndicator[progress, {0, 1}]]
```

If you want it embedded in a notebook or CDF-style interface, wrap the computation so the progress variable is updated by reference:

```wolfram
Manipulate[
 Module[{result},
  progress = 0;
  result = Table[
    progress = i/n;
    Import[files[[i]]],
    {i, n}
  ];
  progress = 1;
  result
 ],
 {{progress, 0}, None},
 TrackedSymbols :> {n},
 SynchronousUpdating -> False
]
```

