If you’re trying to capture the text field value when the button is clicked, the main issue is that the button callback needs to explicitly read the widget’s current value.

In GUIKit, you typically do that by giving the text field a name and then querying its `"text"` property inside the button action.

Example:

```mathematica
Needs["GUIKit`"];

