The issue is that the sphere condition should use r^2, not r.

You want:

F = Piecewise[{{1, Sum[x[i]^2, {i, d}] <= r^2}}, 0];

because a point is inside a sphere of radius r when

x1^2 + x2^2 + ... + xd^2 <= r^2.

Also, for the iterator construction, NIntegrate has HoldAll, so Table[...] must be turned into a Sequence of iterators:

d = 10;
r = 1000;

NIntegrate[
  F,
  Evaluate[Sequence @@ Table[{x[i], -r, r}, {i, d}]],
  Method -> {"MonteCarloRule", "Points" -> 1000000}
]

A cleaner version is:

d = 10;
r = 1000;
F = Boole[Total[Table[x[i]^2, {i, d}]] <= r^2];

NIntegrate[
  F,
  Evaluate[Sequence @@ Table[{x[i], -r, r}, {i, d}]],
  Method -> {"MonteCarloRule", "Points" -> 1000000}
]

This should give the correct 10-dimensional volume of the 9-sphere.

