If your goal is a grid of numbers with grid lines, use `Graphics` directly and place `Text` objects at the cell centers.

### Example

```wl
SeedRandom[1];
m = 10;  (* grid size *)
premade = RandomInteger[10, {m, m}];

col[n_] := Table[{n - 0.5, i - 0.5}, {i, 1, m}];

Graphics[
  {
    Table[
      Text[
        Style[premade[[#, i]], Large, FontFamily -> "Times"],
        col[i][[#]]
      ] & /@ Range[m],
      {i, 1, m}
    ]
  },
  GridLines -> {Range[m], Range[m]},
  PlotRange -> {{0, m}, {0, m}},
  Axes -> False,
  Frame -> True,
  GridLinesStyle -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.8], Dashed]
]
```

### Notes
- `premade` is your matrix of values.
- `col[n_]` computes the positions of text in column `n`.
- `Text[..., {x, y}]` puts each number in the center of a cell.
- `GridLines` and `Frame -> True` give the table-like appearance.

