Use a custom tick specification that wraps each label in a Pane, then Rotate it. The Pane lets you add a horizontal offset so the rotated text can be centered under the tick.

Example:

```wl
myTickList[min_, max_, seg_, shift_?NumericQ, phi_?NumericQ, len_: 0.01] := 
  Table[
    {
      i,
      Rotate[
        Pane[
          Style["y =" <> ToString[i], LineSpacing -> {0, 12}],
          FrameMargins -> {{shift, 0}, {0, 0}}
        ],
        phi
      ],
      {len, 0}
    },
    {i, If[Head[seg] === List, Union[{min, max}, seg], Range[min, max, seg]]}
  ]
