If you mean aligning axis labels consistently across multiple plots, the built-in `AxesLabel` placement in `Plot3D`/`Graphics3D` is view-dependent, so it can shift as the scene changes. For stable alignment, it’s best to place labels manually with `Text`.

Example:

```wl
Graphics3D[
 {
  Text[Style["X", 25, Bold], {1.05, 0, 0}],
  Text[Style["Y", 25, Bold], {0, 1.05, 0}],
  Text[Style["Z", 25, Bold], {0, 0, 1.05}]
