When you use Grid, the displayed size is controlled by the grid cells, not just by the image itself. To export pictures at the “correct” visible size, you usually need to make the image dimensions explicit before putting them in the grid.

Best approach:
- give all images the same ImageSize, or
- resize/pad them to the same bounding box before Grid

Example with fixed-size thumbnails:

```wl
imgs = {
  ImageResize[img1, {100, 100}],
  ImageResize[img2, {100, 100}],
  ImageResize[img3, {100, 100}]
};

g = Grid[
  Partition[imgs, 2, 2, {1, 1}, ""],
  ItemSize -> All,
  Spacings -> {2, 2}
];

Export["grid.png", g]
```

If you want the images to keep their aspect ratio but still fit uniform slots, use padding:

```wl
fitImg[img_, s_: 100] := ImagePad[ImageResize[img, s], s, White];

g = Grid[
  {
    {fitImg[img1], fitImg[img2]},
    {fitImg[img3], fitImg[img4]}
  },
  Spacings -> {0, 0}
];

Export["grid.png", g]
```

If the issue is that export changes the apparent size, another useful tactic is to set the final image size on export:

```wl
Export["grid.png", g, ImageResolution -> 300]
```

But the key point is: standardize the images first, then Grid will export them consistently.

