If you want a function to “behave more like `Plot`,” the usual approach is to make it a single `Piecewise` function.

`Plot` is great at handling multiple branches visually, but if your expression is really one function with different formulas on different intervals, `Piecewise` is the cleanest way to encode that behavior:

```wl
pw = Piecewise[{
   {2 Sqrt[x], 0 <= x <= 1},
   {4 - 2 x,   1 < x < 2.5},
   {2 x - 7,   2.5 <= x <= 4}
