Inside `Module`, the symbol name is localized, but the front end/debugger can still show the global symbol value unless you inspect the module’s local context specifically. So it can look like the local variable “leaks” into Global, when in fact you’re just viewing the wrong scope.

Use the debugger’s:

- Stack
- Local variables

to see the actual `Module`-local value.

Example:

```wl
Clear[i];
i = 12;

f[] := Module[{i},
  For[i = 1, i < 10, i++,
    Print[i];
    Print[":"];
    Print[i/0]
  ]
];

f[]
```

If you stop at a breakpoint/message inside `f`, the global `i` may still be visible elsewhere, but the module-local `i` is the one shown under Local variables.

