For a piecewise parametric curve, the easiest way is usually to split it into separate plotted pieces and assign `PlotStyle` colors to each piece.

Example:

```wl
ParametricPlot[
 {
  {Cos[t], Sin[t]},
  {Cos[t], 2 Sin[t]},
  {Cos[t], 3 Sin[t]}
 },
 {t, 0, 2 Pi},
 PlotStyle -> {Red, Blue, Green}
]
```

If the curve is genuinely piecewise in one expression, define each segment separately and plot them together:

```wl
p1 = {Cos[t], Sin[t]};
p2 = {Cos[t], 2 Sin[t]};

ParametricPlot[
 Evaluate@{p1, p2},
 {t, 0, 2 Pi},
 PlotStyle -> {Red, Blue}
]
```

If you want colors chosen automatically from a palette:

```wl
curves = {
  {Cos[t], Sin[t]},
  {Cos[t], 2 Sin[t]},
  {Cos[t], 3 Sin[t]}
};

ParametricPlot[
 curves,
 {t, 0, 2 Pi},
 PlotStyle -> ColorData[97] /@ Range[Length[curves]]
]
```

If you need one piecewise parametric curve defined by conditions on `t`, a good pattern is:

```wl
ParametricPlot[
 Evaluate@{
   {Cos[t], Sin[t]} /. t -> t /; 0 <= t <= Pi,
   {Cos[t], 2 Sin[t]} /. t -> t /; Pi < t <= 2 Pi
 },
 {t, 0, 2 Pi},
 PlotStyle -> {Red, Blue}
]
```

