What’s likely happening is that the code inside your Dynamic/Button is being evaluated in the normal notebook/front-end way, and the front end can interrupt or appear to “stall” long-running actions.

Key point from the resolved case: if you’re trying to print or notify after a delay, don’t rely on the button evaluation itself to stay active for a long time. Also, `EvaluationCompletionAction` won’t help you determine elapsed time, since it only runs after completion.

A more reliable pattern is to keep the button lightweight and move the work into a separate evaluation or scheduled task.

Example:

```wl
Button["Run",
  CreateScheduledTask[
    Module[{result},
      result = yourExpression;
      Print[result];
    ],
    {}
  ] // StartScheduledTask
]
```

If you just want to print something after the computation finishes, you can also do:

