If you want to merge two lists and keep the elements they have in common, the efficient way is to use their intersection first, then use that to pick or combine matching entries.

For simple lists:
```wolfram
common = Intersection[list1, list2];
```

If your lists are like `{date, value}` pairs and you want the rows with matching dates:
```wolfram
commonDates = Intersection[list1[[All, 1]], list2[[All, 1]]];

commonItems1 = Select[list1, MemberQ[commonDates, #[[1]]] &];
commonItems2 = Select[list2, MemberQ[commonDates, #[[1]]] &];
```

If you want to merge matching records by their first element:
```wolfram
assoc1 = AssociationThread[list1[[All, 1]] -> list1[[All, 2 ;;]]];
assoc2 = AssociationThread[list2[[All, 1]] -> list2[[All, 2 ;;]]];

combined = KeyValueMap[
  {#1, assoc1[#1], assoc2[#1]} &,
  KeyIntersection[{assoc1, assoc2}]
];
```

If the lists are already sorted and aligned, this can often be simplified further.

