1. start on window opening  
2. start when a checkbox/toggle changes  
3. start from `Dynamic` without visible controls  
4. start from a menu item or palette action

To add tangent/velocity vectors to a plotted space curve, evaluate the curve and its derivative at the parameter value of each point, then draw arrows from those points.

For a 3D parametric curve `r[t]`, use `ParametricPlot3D` plus `Graphics3D`:

```mathematica
r[t_] := {Cos[t], Sin[t], t/2};

Manipulate[
 Module[{p = r[t0], v = D[r[t], t] /. t -> t0},
  Show[
   ParametricPlot3D[r[t], {t, 0, 6 Pi}, PlotStyle -> Blue],
   Graphics3D[
    {
     Red, PointSize[Large], Point[p],
     Black, Arrow[{p, p + 0.7 Normalize[v]}]
    }
   ],
   PlotRange -> All
  ]
 ],
 {t0, 0, 6 Pi}
]
```

If you want several tangent vectors along the curve:

```mathematica
r[t_] := {Cos[t], Sin[t], t/2};

Show[
 ParametricPlot3D[r[t], {t, 0, 6 Pi}, PlotStyle -> Blue],
 Graphics3D[
  Table[
   With[{p = r[t], v = D[r[s], s] /. s -> t},
    Arrow[{p, p + 0.7 Normalize[v]}]
   ],
   {t, 0, 6 Pi, Pi}
  ]
 ]
]
```

If you want just the tangent line at a point instead of an arrow:

```mathematica
Graphics3D[
 {
  Red, PointSize[Large], Point[p],
  Black, Line[{p - 2 Normalize[v], p + 2 Normalize[v]}]
 }
]
```

